Below is one possible way to prevent the “default‐flow” from being unset when a catch‐event is dropped onto a non‐default branch.  Rather than listening for every single `connection.delete` (which will also fire during a reconnect/split), we only unset the default when the user explicitly deletes a flow (i.e. in the `elements.delete` command).

