```

Explanation of the change:

1. We stop unsetting the `default` attribute on every low-level `connection.delete` (which also fires during reconnects/splits).
2. Instead, we only react to the higher-level `elements.delete` command—which is what the user triggers to remove a flow.
3. This way, dropping (and splitting) a catch event onto a non-default branch will no longer inadvertently remove the gateway’s default flow.
